WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:16.789
SCAMMING AMAZON:
It’s no secret that people aren’t exactly

00:00:16.789 --> 00:00:18.100
fans of big tech.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:24.289
They don’t like Facebook, they don’t like
Google, and they especially don’t like Amazon.

00:00:24.289 --> 00:00:29.670
Usually, the primary critique against Amazon
is the way they run their business.

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:34.660
Amazon has become infamous for cutthroat rules
and miserable working conditions.

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:38.989
Their drivers often have to pee in bottles
while their warehouse workers are often left

00:00:38.989 --> 00:00:40.840
with chronic pain.

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:46.640
This is why many Amazon warehouses have turnovers
rates that are over 100%.

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:50.380
Amazon has never really worried too much about
this as they’ve found that high turnover

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:53.559
is actually a good thing at warehouses.

00:00:53.559 --> 00:00:57.800
It turns out that people are usually more
motivated and productive when they get a new

00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:00.130
warehouse job than they are a few months in.

00:01:00.130 --> 00:01:05.230
So, it’s actually in Amazon’s best interest
to keep things churning as long as there’s

00:01:05.230 --> 00:01:06.720
enough people to churn through of course.

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:11.619
Hearing all this, I’m sure most of you have
some level of distaste for the meat grinder

00:01:11.619 --> 00:01:13.000
that is Amazon.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:17.810
But, many of our peers have actually been
taking this distaste to the next level.

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:22.710
They’re not just complaining about it on
the internet or advocating for unions.

00:01:22.710 --> 00:01:27.080
Instead, they’re actually stealing from
and defrauding Amazon.

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:31.340
The worst offenders rack up stolen merchandise
in the hundreds of thousands of dollars and

00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:33.450
even over a million dollars.

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:38.090
While these are the people who make the news,
there are tens of thousands and maybe even

00:01:38.090 --> 00:01:42.390
hundreds of thousands of everyday people who
pulling off the same scam on a much smaller

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:43.390
basis.

00:01:43.390 --> 00:01:47.220
These guys usually have $500 or a $1000 worth
of stolen merchandise.

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:52.520
So, here’s exactly how people have been
stealing from one of the largest companies

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:54.049
in the world.

00:01:54.049 --> 00:01:59.540
RETURN SCAM EXPLAINED:
Getting straight into it, the overview of

00:01:59.540 --> 00:02:02.640
the scam isn’t all that hard to understand.

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:06.979
Essentially, people have been abusing Amazon’s
generous return policy to get unjustified

00:02:06.979 --> 00:02:08.500
refunds on products.

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:12.800
While simple in nature, there’s actually
a bunch of nuances that are involved in making

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:16.510
this scam work because Amazon is of course
not stupid.

00:02:16.510 --> 00:02:20.690
They’re well aware of this scam and they’re
constantly tightening their procedures and

00:02:20.690 --> 00:02:22.910
protocols to minimize its occurrence.

00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:27.849
Nonetheless, many everyday people are still
benefiting from this scam thanks to the existence

00:02:27.849 --> 00:02:29.730
of full on scam businesses.

00:02:29.730 --> 00:02:33.720
I’m sure you’ve heard about the classic
gift card scammers that will email you or

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:36.690
call you pretending to be Apple, Amazon, or
Microsoft.

00:02:36.690 --> 00:02:41.020
They’ll usually tell you that your computer
has some sort of virus, and that you need

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:43.769
to pay them in the form of gift cards to fix
it.

00:02:43.769 --> 00:02:47.200
If you’re interested in the innerworkings
of these scams, I would recommend that you

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:49.010
check out Jim Browning’s videos on them.

00:02:49.010 --> 00:02:52.650
But, anyway, some of these scammers have switched
strategies.

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:56.980
Instead of scamming everyday people, they’ve
pivoted to helping everyday people scam Amazon.

00:02:56.980 --> 00:03:01.520
Usually, they’ll set up a discord community
that’s filled with a couple of scammers.

00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:05.790
Then, they’ll go out and discretely promote
their servers online.

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:11.680
Really, they don’t need that much attention,
they just need 5 or 10 people to join up.

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:14.989
From there, the servers usually grow through
word of mouth.

00:03:14.989 --> 00:03:19.459
Once these 5 or 10 people get products for
a super low price, they often tell their friends

00:03:19.459 --> 00:03:24.659
about it, and within no time, these servers
end up boasting thousands of users.

00:03:24.659 --> 00:03:29.099
All these users have to do is tell the scammers
what product they want and the scammers will

00:03:29.099 --> 00:03:33.260
get it for them for a 70 or 80% discount.

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:37.959
Usually, the scammers will start off by creating
a fake amazon account on your behalf.

00:03:37.959 --> 00:03:41.980
From there, they’ll use gift cards or stolen
credit cards to order a bunch of merchandise

00:03:41.980 --> 00:03:45.190
to an AirBnB or some sort of temporary address.

00:03:45.190 --> 00:03:50.659
Nowadays, almost all the couriers take pictures
of the delivered product, so these scammers

00:03:50.659 --> 00:03:55.810
often meet the delivery drivers outside the
AirBnB to prevent them from taking a picture.

00:03:55.810 --> 00:03:59.909
This makes it especially easy for them to
turn around and convince Amazon that the product

00:03:59.909 --> 00:04:02.770
was never delivered and get a refund.

00:04:02.770 --> 00:04:06.520
From there, they’ll ship it to the discord
member who requested the product and the scammers

00:04:06.520 --> 00:04:09.850
will keep the 20 or 30% that the member did
pay for the product.

00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:13.010
This strategy generally only works on cheaper
products though.

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:17.400
When it comes to more expensive products,
the scammers have to turn to a different strategy.

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:20.519
The first part of the scam works exactly the
same.

00:04:20.519 --> 00:04:25.520
They’ll use a fake account and fake credentials
to order a product, but this time, they wont

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:28.070
try to convince Amazon that the product wasn’t
delivered.

00:04:28.070 --> 00:04:33.300
Instead, they’ll take the product, replace
it with a fake counterfeit and return it.

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:36.960
This scheme is especially common with Apple’s
AirPods Max.

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:42.620
The stickerprice of the headphones is $550,
but you can buy an extremely convincing replica

00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:48.020
for just a $120 on Alibaba which is about
22% of the price.

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:53.960
This gives the scammers plenty of margin to
give the discord member a 60 or 70% discount.

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:56.810
And that’s exactly how they pull off this
scam.

00:04:56.810 --> 00:05:03.470
THIS IS MESSED UP:
Throughout the pandemic, this scam has exploded

00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:07.840
in popularity especially amongst college students
and broke young adults.

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:13.120
But, for obvious reasons, engaging in this
scam is a horrible idea.

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:14.979
First of all, there’s the whole moral dilemma.

00:05:14.979 --> 00:05:19.840
You’re essentially stealing products from
Amazon and/or Amazon sellers.

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:24.630
Given that most people go to discord scammers
and get them to do the dirty work, this is

00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:28.020
obviously not something that they’re willing
to do themselves.

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:32.880
And if you can tell that something is unethical
to do yourself, you probably shouldn’t be

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:35.270
getting someone else to do it for you.

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:39.620
Some of these people like to argue that they’re
just getting back at the evil trillion dollar

00:05:39.620 --> 00:05:44.990
corporation that is Amazon, but this is just
an excuse to justify their actions.

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:48.580
Really, they’re not getting back at Amazon
at all.

00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:52.970
If anything, they’re making the lives of
Amazon employees even worse.

00:05:52.970 --> 00:05:57.190
Here’s the thing, what do you think Amazon
is going to do if a delivery driver racks

00:05:57.190 --> 00:06:00.169
up a record of quote on quote “lost deliveries”.

00:06:00.169 --> 00:06:02.710
They’re obviously going to fire them.

00:06:02.710 --> 00:06:06.750
Not to mention, the cost of stolen products
usually end up coming out of the paychecks

00:06:06.750 --> 00:06:08.460
of Amazon employees.

00:06:08.460 --> 00:06:13.560
While Amazon gets a lot of slack for not paying
employees enough, the truth isn’t that Amazon

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:18.800
doesn’t want to pay employees more, it’s
that they simply cannot afford to pay more.

00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:25.190
Yes, Jeff Bezos is one of the richest people
in the world, but all of that is stock value.

00:06:25.190 --> 00:06:30.090
When it comes to actual cashflow, Amazon literally
has negative cash flow.

00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:34.930
For decades, they’ve been using AWS to subsidize
their retail business which has basically

00:06:34.930 --> 00:06:36.850
never been profitable.

00:06:36.850 --> 00:06:41.060
With that being said though, Amazon has never
really strived for profitability either.

00:06:41.060 --> 00:06:45.410
They’d rather just maintain a breakeven
income statement and reinvest everything into

00:06:45.410 --> 00:06:49.210
new warehouses, logistics channels, and of
course employees.

00:06:49.210 --> 00:06:53.750
And the people who are stealing from Amazon
are directly preventing this from happening.

00:06:53.750 --> 00:06:59.250
Now, you may not think that this would make
that big of a difference, but that’s completely

00:06:59.250 --> 00:07:00.250
false.

00:07:00.250 --> 00:07:06.330
In 2021, a record $761 billion worth of merchandise
was returned.

00:07:06.330 --> 00:07:10.930
And out of this, a whopping 10.3% of returns
were fraudulent.

00:07:10.930 --> 00:07:16.819
That translates to $78.3 billion every single
year, and that’s just the ones that are

00:07:16.819 --> 00:07:17.819
caught.

00:07:17.819 --> 00:07:22.349
The good scams go completely undetected, so
the percentage of fraudulent returns is probably

00:07:22.349 --> 00:07:24.669
closer to 15 or 20%.

00:07:24.669 --> 00:07:29.810
But, even if we assume 10%, this works out
to billions of dollars per year for Amazon

00:07:29.810 --> 00:07:30.910
alone.

00:07:30.910 --> 00:07:36.660
The average Amazon return rate stands at 5
to 15% depending on the category and season.

00:07:36.660 --> 00:07:39.360
We can just estimate in the middle and call
it 10%.

00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:45.830
If 10% of Amazon orders are returned and 10%
of those returns are fraudulent, Amazon is

00:07:45.830 --> 00:07:49.319
being defrauded on roughly 1% of their top
line revenue.

00:07:49.319 --> 00:07:56.530
In 2021, Amazon had net sales of $279 billion
in North America and $127 billion internationally

00:07:56.530 --> 00:07:59.310
which adds up to a total of $406 billion.

00:07:59.310 --> 00:08:05.080
Now, that’s net sales meaning that it already
accounts for the revenue loss due to returns.

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:09.080
This means that their top line number was
roughly $450 billion.

00:08:09.080 --> 00:08:15.420
Using our fraud estimate of 1%, Amazon lost
approximately $4.5 billion last year due to

00:08:15.420 --> 00:08:17.599
return frauds and stolen goods.

00:08:17.599 --> 00:08:20.780
And there’s only two ways that Amazon can
pay for this.

00:08:20.780 --> 00:08:24.980
They can either increase prices or decrease
salaries.

00:08:24.980 --> 00:08:30.129
And given their history, we know that they’d
rather decrease salaries than increase prices.

00:08:30.129 --> 00:08:34.349
Currently, Amazon has a total of 1.6 million
employees.

00:08:34.349 --> 00:08:38.529
If this money had gone towards their paychecks,
each and every one of them could have earned

00:08:38.529 --> 00:08:41.050
an extra $2800 last year.

00:08:41.050 --> 00:08:44.839
It’s not just Amazon employees that are
being hurt either.

00:08:44.839 --> 00:08:48.120
Random customers and sellers are also feeling
the pain.

00:08:48.120 --> 00:08:52.630
First of all, some random person is going
to become a victim of credit card fraud.

00:08:52.630 --> 00:08:57.400
After that, once the douchebag scammer returns
the fake pair of AirPods Max, it’s more

00:08:57.400 --> 00:09:01.880
than likely that some other Amazon customer
is going to end up with that junk even though

00:09:01.880 --> 00:09:03.450
they paid the full $550.

00:09:03.450 --> 00:09:09.459
When they realize this, they’re gonna have
to call Amazon and explain the situation,

00:09:09.459 --> 00:09:13.940
and Amazon is probably going to turn around
and flag the sellers account and the customer

00:09:13.940 --> 00:09:16.070
will probably go leave a terrible review.

00:09:16.070 --> 00:09:20.610
And if this happens a few times, Amazon will
probably ban the seller thinking that they're

00:09:20.610 --> 00:09:22.490
a counterfeit product seller.

00:09:22.490 --> 00:09:26.300
So, in the end, you’re left with Amazon
employees who are getting the short end of

00:09:26.300 --> 00:09:29.980
the stick, you have victims of credit card
fraud, you have customers with fake products

00:09:29.980 --> 00:09:35.190
and a nightmare buying experience, and you
have a seller who just lost their small business.

00:09:35.190 --> 00:09:39.400
And all of this is just so that some broke
losers across the country can flex to their

00:09:39.400 --> 00:09:42.540
friends with products that they can’t afford.

00:09:42.540 --> 00:09:46.579
When you think about it, it’s really quite
messed up.

00:09:46.579 --> 00:09:51.032
A SPREADING PARASITE:
The worst part of all of this is that this

00:09:51.032 --> 00:09:54.570
scam is no longer unique to Amazon.

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:58.140
Virutally every retailer has gotten into the
online game and they’re all dealing with

00:09:58.140 --> 00:10:01.290
the same issue whether it be Best Buy or Gucci.

00:10:01.290 --> 00:10:05.110
This scam is even starting to spread into
other industries as well such as food and

00:10:05.110 --> 00:10:06.110
grocery delivery.

00:10:06.110 --> 00:10:12.730
This server, for example is offering 80% off
on grocery delivery and 55% off on food delivery.

00:10:12.730 --> 00:10:16.890
To accomplish this, the scammers just charge
the entire amount onto a stolen credit card

00:10:16.890 --> 00:10:17.890
number.

00:10:17.890 --> 00:10:21.960
And, it’s up to the fraud victim to file
for credit card fraud and get a refund.

00:10:21.960 --> 00:10:26.550
Usually, the refund is issued by the credit
card company or the food delivery app.

00:10:26.550 --> 00:10:30.430
Fortunately, the delivery driver still gets
paid for the delivery even if the order is

00:10:30.430 --> 00:10:32.290
refunded in most cases.

00:10:32.290 --> 00:10:35.640
But, once again, someone has to pay for this.

00:10:35.640 --> 00:10:39.880
Usually, this just leads to higher prices
across food delivery apps and the apps taking

00:10:39.880 --> 00:10:43.480
a larger portion of the revenue from both
the restaurant and the driver.

00:10:43.480 --> 00:10:46.480
If the credit card company fronts the cost,
you have a similar conundrum.

00:10:46.480 --> 00:10:52.290
They’re gonna try to make this money back
by raising their 23% interest rates to 25%.

00:10:52.290 --> 00:10:56.680
And given that the average American has nearly
$6000 in credit card debt, these scammers

00:10:56.680 --> 00:10:59.589
aren’t doing the country any favors.

00:10:59.589 --> 00:11:05.440
The worst part about all this is that this
scam is only possible because of us.

00:11:05.440 --> 00:11:08.389
Traditional scams just require a scammer and
a victim.

00:11:08.389 --> 00:11:12.600
But, this scam requires, a scammer, a victim,
and a customer.

00:11:12.600 --> 00:11:15.630
Without a customer, it cannot operate.

00:11:15.630 --> 00:11:19.510
And these customers aren’t random people
in third world countries.

00:11:19.510 --> 00:11:25.250
These customers are our neighbors, our classmates,
our friends, and it might even be you.

00:11:25.250 --> 00:11:29.320
Also, it’s not like these people are stealing
for survival either.

00:11:29.320 --> 00:11:32.680
After all, they’re not stealing a loaf of
bread or eggs.

00:11:32.680 --> 00:11:37.649
Instead they’re stealing high value tech
products like computers, laptops, and phones.

00:11:37.649 --> 00:11:41.660
Or they’re stealing convenience services
that they don’t want to pay for like food

00:11:41.660 --> 00:11:43.060
and grocery delivery.

00:11:43.060 --> 00:11:48.750
And in the end, how can we honestly criticize
these big tech companies and evil businesses

00:11:48.750 --> 00:11:53.010
when many of our peers are engaging in the
same activities when given the opportunity.

00:11:53.010 --> 00:11:58.100
Now, I’m not suggesting that we should let
the big companies off the hook.

00:11:58.100 --> 00:12:03.000
I’m just suggesting that we should try to
clean up our side as well, but that’s just

00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:04.000
what I think.

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:05.670
Were you familiar with this scam?

00:12:05.670 --> 00:12:06.990
Comment that down below.

